[38;5;231m⏺[39m Fixed — one-character change in [38;5;153msrc/textkit/chunking.py:18[39m.

  [1mRoot cause:[0m the loop advances by [38;5;153mchunk_size[39m ([38;5;153mrange(0, len(text), chunk_size)[39m) but the slice ended at [38;5;153mi + chunk_size -
[39m  [38;5;153m1[39m. The stride and the slice width disagreed by one, so the last character of every chunk was silently dropped.
  [38;5;153mchunk_text("abcdef", 2)[39m returned [38;5;153m['a', 'c', 'e'][39m; with [38;5;153mchunk_size=1[39m it would have returned a list of empty strings.

  [1mFix:[0m [38;5;153mtext[i:i + chunk_size][39m.

  [1mVerification:[0m the two existing failing tests ([38;5;153mtest_chunk_text_even_split[39m, [38;5;153mtest_chunk_text_uneven_tail[39m) reproduced the
  bug before the change; after it, [38;5;153mpytest[39m reports 6 passed, and [38;5;153mruff[39m and [38;5;153mmypy[39m are clean on the file. No new tests were
  added — the suite already covered the even-split, uneven-tail, oversized-chunk, empty-string, and invalid-[38;5;153mchunk_size[39m
  cases.

